{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 126, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge 3 with a 3x3 conv restores connectivity and gives large gains, unlike replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where edge 3 was none gains more than swapping from an existing conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With the direct 0->3 edge absent, a skip on edge 5 helps gradient/information flow to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a skip on edge 5 with a conv hurts a lot when edge 3 is none, since the skip was the key path."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 when edge 3 is already none cuts most paths from input and hurts more than usual."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip on edge 0 to a conv gives large gains in parameter-free parents."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling edge with a conv yields consistent gains on all datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a skip on edge 3 with a conv loses accuracy, whereas replacing none gains."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling with conv on edge 5 gains on all datasets, unlike replacing skip or 1x1 where ImageNet16 drops."}, {"edit_edge": 3